    "updated_at": "2026-06-25T21:33:46Z",
    "body": "FWIW something like this can be done to have the same behavior as the `<select>` in chome:\n```html\n<button id=\"btn\" commandfor=\"p\" command=\"toggle-popover\">toggle show down</button>\n<div id=\"p\" popover>Bar</div>\n<script>\n  let flag = false;\n  btn.addEventListener('pointerdown', (e) => {\n    if (e.pointerType === 'mouse') {\n      flag = false;\n      if (!btn.disabled && !p.matches(':popover-open')) {\n        popover.showPopover({\n          source: btn\n        });\n        flag = true;\n      }\n    }\n  });\n  btn.addEventListener('click', (e) => {\n    if (e.pointerType === 'mouse') {\n      if (flag) {\n        e.preventDefault();\n        flag = false;\n      }\n    }\n  });\n</script>\n```\nor using `commandfor` alone and coding all types of interactions.",
